  </div>

  <div style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding-block: 1.5rem;">
    <div class="directory-grid plate-card-grid oeuvre-directory-grid">
      <a href="#components">
        <h3 class="oeuvre-card-title">
          <span>LES DOSSIERS</span>
          <span class="fi-caption-box"><span class="fi-prompt-marker">&gt;</span> RECORDS (24)</span>
        </h3>
      </a>
      <a href="#components">
        <h3 class="oeuvre-card-title">
          <span>LES MANUSCRITS</span>
          <span class="fi-caption-box"><span class="fi-prompt-marker">&gt;</span> MANUSCRIPTS (4)</span>
        </h3>
      </a>
      <a href="#components">
        <h3 class="oeuvre-card-title">
          <span>LES RAPPORTS</span>
          <span class="fi-caption-box"><span class="fi-prompt-marker">&gt;</span> ATLAS REPORTS (11)</span>
        </h3>
      </a>
      <a href="#components">
        <h3 class="oeuvre-card-title">
          <span>LA DOCTRINE</span>
          <span class="fi-caption-box"><span class="fi-prompt-marker">&gt;</span> SYSTEMS DOCTRINE (6)</span>
        </h3>
      </a>
      <a href="#components">
        <h3 class="oeuvre-card-title">
          <span>LA PROVENANCE</span>
          <span class="fi-caption-box"><span class="fi-prompt-marker">&gt;</span> SOURCE CHAIN</span>
        </h3>
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-sm text-fi-slate">.directory-grid.plate-card-grid &middot; the route's primary navigation instrument: large label + one right-aligned SYSOUT plate per card. The grid carries <strong>one card per public shelf</strong> &mdash; the count follows the architecture dossier, never a fixed cap. L'Œuvre's five sit on a 6-column field as 2+2+2 over 3+3.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding-block: 1.5rem;">
    <div class="object-motion-strip">
      <p class="section-label">Motion evidence</p>
      <figure class="object-motion-figure">
        <video controls preload="metadata" playsinline></video>
        <figcaption>FI-PHOTO-001 / Initial local archive photo batch / source footage 1</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-sm text-fi-slate">.object-motion-strip + .object-motion-figure &middot; source footage on an object record, kept out of the still-photo strip because a clip is not a photograph &mdash; same plate and caption rule as .object-primary-figure</p>
  </div>

  <div style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding-block: 1.5rem;">
    <p style="margin: 0;"><a href="/styleguide/">Primary link</a> &mdash; blueprint cyan, underlined, turns green on hover.</p>
    <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-sm text-fi-slate">a &middot; color --blueprint, hover --fi-green</p>
  </div>

  <div style="padding-block: 1.5rem;">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center" style="gap: 1rem;">
      <button type="button" style="border: 1px solid var(--fi-cyan-border); background: var(--fi-surface); color: var(--ink); font-family: var(--font-system); padding: 0.5rem 1rem; text-transform: uppercase;">Focusable Button</button>
      <a href="/styleguide/">Focusable link</a>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-sm text-fi-slate">focus state &middot; tab here for the 3px --focus (cyan) outline shared by every interactive element</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-inner" style="padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem); border-top: 1px solid var(--line);" aria-labelledby="heuristics">
  <p class="section-label">&gt; 04 / Heuristics</p>
  <h2 id="heuristics" style="color: var(--fi-cyan); font-family: var(--font-system); font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase;">Heuristics</h2>
  <ul style="max-width: 70ch; margin: 1rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.2rem; color: var(--ink); font-family: var(--font-ui); font-size: 1.08rem; line-height: 1.7;">
    <li>Dark archive field first: a black <span class="font-mono">--fi-bg</span> background under a faint fixed scan-grid and scanline. High contrast, hard-edged offset shadows, no rounded corners.</li>
    <li>Space Mono is the default system voice. Old Standard TT and Courier Prime carry human and authored warmth; IBM Plex Sans carries report body copy.</li>
    <li>Color is role-based: cyan is structure, green is SYSOUT machine output, magenta is prompt syntax used sparingly, gold / amber / copper are human and provenance warmth, maroon and silver are the institutional register.</li>
    <li>Structure is shared across sibling routes; only the color temperature changes, set by a body class per route family.</li>
    <li>Sentence case for prose; Title Case for labels, headings, and menu items. Years and machine output stay uppercase mono.</li>
    <li>Caption boxes are machine output &mdash; labels, counts, statuses, declarations. Never use them for prose.</li>
    <li>Accessibility: a skip link, a 3px cyan focus outline on every interactive element, and <span class="font-mono">prefers-reduced-motion</span> to disable the animated mark sheen.</li>
    <li>Bilingual register: French route names (L'Œuvre, Le Signal, À Propos) paired with English and SYSOUT captions.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="tagline" style="max-width: 64ch; margin-top: 2rem; color: var(--brass); font-style: italic;">A thing documented is a thing not yet lost.</p>
</section>
